## Project Architecture

- **Product**: Superplan
- **Shape**: Global Agent Skills pack + POSIX installer + data-only planning hubs
- **Platforms**: macOS and Linux (POSIX). Windows is out of scope until asked.
- **Primary language**: POSIX shell (`install.sh`, tests) + Markdown (`SKILL.md`)
- **Build / verify**: `make verify` (= lint + test + build/pack-check)

```
superplan/
  skills/                 # published pack (global install source)
  templates/hub/          # data-only hub templates (no skill copies)
  install.sh              # humanize-style agent-select installer
  tests/                  # installer + pack checks
  .cursor/rules/          # how we build Superplan
  .cursor/skills/         # plan → execute → complete for THIS repo
  planning/phases/        # sequence of record for Superplan itself
```

Two skill trees, never mixed:

1. **`.cursor/skills/`** — loop for building Superplan (this repo).
2. **`skills/`** — the pack users install globally. After install, those skills
   run from any product repo or planning hub.

Node is not a Superplan runtime. It is only the consumer toolchain for
`npx skills add` (skills.sh). Superplan is not a Go app.

### Inspiration sources

- ColonyX Claude port: `/Users/aman/projects/Claude Plans/ColonyX`
- Original methodology: https://github.com/commoddity/turboplan
- Installer shape: https://github.com/harshaneel/humanize/blob/main/install.sh

### Build & Run

```bash
make verify          # lint (shellcheck) + test + pack-check
make install-hooks   # lefthook: pre-commit → make verify
./install.sh --help  # after the skeleton task; real install is a later task
```

Toolchain baseline (host, 2026-09): Node v22.18.0 (npx skills consumer only);
shellcheck 0.11.0 and lefthook 2.1.14 via Homebrew.

